<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>R001 depends_on without health condition · eyeship</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.b6f3a01e.css">
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="top"><a class="brand" href="/">eyeship</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="/">Deployments</a><a href="/rules" aria-current="page">Rules</a></nav></header>
<main id="main">
<p class="sub"><a href="/rules">Rules</a></p><h1><code>R001</code> depends_on without health condition</h1><p>Default severity: <span class="badge warning">warning</span></p><h3>Failure scenario</h3><p>With the short list syntax or `condition: service_started`, the dependent service starts as soon as its dependency is launched, not when it is ready. It gets connection refused at startup and crashes.</p><h3>Fix</h3><p>Use `condition: service_healthy` and give the dependency a healthcheck.</p><h3>Bad example</h3><pre><code>services:
  api:
    image: acme/api:1.4.2
    depends_on:
      - db
  db:
    image: postgres:16.4
</code></pre><h3>Good example</h3><pre><code>services:
  api:
    image: acme/api:1.4.2
    depends_on:
      db:
        condition: service_healthy
  db:
    image: postgres:16.4
    healthcheck:
      test: [&quot;CMD-SHELL&quot;, &quot;pg_isready -U postgres&quot;]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5
</code></pre></main>
<footer>eyeship 0.1.0 · static audit, nothing was run</footer>
</body>
</html>
